WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.139
Some things are best kept contained.

00:00:03.139 --> 00:00:08.230
After all, this is the founding principle
behind the SCP Foundation themselves, to secure

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:12.330
and contain the most dangerous anomalies in
order to protect human lives.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:17.849
But within the Foundation itself, are things
which should never be uncovered, secrets that

00:00:17.849 --> 00:00:19.890
must never be told.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:24.789
Secured behind multiple layers of containment
like the Seven Seals of Revelation, is a threat

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:30.419
so high level in its nature that it can’t
even be given a class: SCP-5999.

00:00:30.419 --> 00:00:37.550
But in order to truly understand this late
series SCP, we have to go all the way back

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.290
to one of the earliest.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:44.170
Anyone looking for SCP-001 will quickly realize
that there are several different entities

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.050
and anomalies that share this designation.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:50.040
Many reasons have been given for this classification
quirk.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.850
Perhaps they were all discovered in the early
days of the Foundation, before the current

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.180
numbering system was introduced.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:01.270
Others have suggested that the many different
SCP-001s are an intentional misdirection by

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:07.579
the Foundation, to keep the nature of the
true first SCP a closely-guarded secret.

00:01:07.579 --> 00:01:14.969
One of the many entries, and the one we’ll
be referring to as SCP-001 to understand SCP-5999,

00:01:14.969 --> 00:01:18.159
is otherwise known as ‘The Database’.

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:23.100
Information about The Database is kept a secret
to the entire SCP Foundation apart from the

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.670
Overseer Council.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:26.090
The reason behind this?

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:32.969
Well, that would be because this SCP-001 contains
details of the very nature of the Foundation

00:01:32.969 --> 00:01:36.180
itself, including its creation.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:42.170
Not how the organization was founded, mind
you; how it was created, and by whom.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:47.389
We’re about to break the most powerful layer
of containment of all: The fourth wall.

00:01:47.389 --> 00:01:53.170
You see, to you or I, the SCP Foundation and
its vast catalogue of user generated articles

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:57.719
on the creative and the creepy are nothing
more than a source of entertainment.

00:01:57.719 --> 00:02:03.579
It can be fun to study the lore and the nuances
of different SCPs, appreciating the imagination

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:06.549
and hard work that the authors put into writing
them.

00:02:06.549 --> 00:02:11.260
It can even inspire us, fuel our own written
endeavors, whether that takes the form of

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:16.750
fan fiction, independent stories, original
SCPs or even a YouTube series.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:22.519
But, when all is said and done, we all know
that the SCP Foundation is fictional.

00:02:22.519 --> 00:02:23.930
And they know it too.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:28.291
Pieced together from various fragments of
information within their own archives, The

00:02:28.291 --> 00:02:33.099
Database contains everything the Foundation
knows about the real world authors of the

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:34.769
SCP Wiki.

00:02:34.769 --> 00:02:39.709
Just like we told you, it’s time to wave
a fond farewell to the fourth wall, the metaphorical

00:02:39.709 --> 00:02:45.270
barrier that separates what we know to be
real from what we know to be purely fiction.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:49.569
The fact that they exist in this fictional
capacity is something the Overseer Council

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:54.650
hopes to hide from the rest of the Foundation’s
personnel, but they also have plans in mind

00:02:54.650 --> 00:03:00.219
for the SCP Wiki writers responsible for creating
them and expanding the roster of anomalies

00:03:00.219 --> 00:03:01.740
they keep contained.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:08.719
The SCP Wiki entry on SCP-001 The Database
closes with a proposal, a plan from the O5

00:03:08.719 --> 00:03:13.610
Council to reach the wiki’s authors in the
real world, through memetic kill agents that

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:16.310
will put them to sleep and then kill them.

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:20.500
With that important background context in
mind, now let’s go all the way back to the

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:25.829
other end of the SCP wiki and take a look
at SCP-5999.

00:03:25.829 --> 00:03:30.939
When first accessing the file, you, the reader,
will notice a few format differences between

00:03:30.939 --> 00:03:34.549
this entry and others within the SCP Archive.

00:03:34.549 --> 00:03:40.250
Each section of SCP-5999 is hidden behind
an encryption, and accessing these will reveal

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.170
the different ‘levels’ of this entry.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:47.080
Remember how we mentioned the Seven Seals
of Revelation at the start of this video?

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.609
That wasn’t a coincidence.

00:03:48.609 --> 00:03:53.890
In the Bible’s Book of Revelation, there
are seven symbolic seals securing a book that

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.500
John of Patmos saw in his vision of the apocalypse.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:02.340
When these seven seals are broken, and the
book is opened, this symbolizes the Second

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:07.129
Coming of the Messiah and marks the beginning
of the biblical apocalypse.

00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:13.930
In much the same vein, SCP-5999 is sealed
in seven different parts, each behind its

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:17.780
own encryption, culminating in one apocalyptic
ending.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:24.100
So, at this point you are probably thinking,
what actually is SCP-5999?

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:28.370
What could be so dangerous that it has to
stay hidden in multiple segments?

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:32.940
Well, on the surface, SCP-5999 is just a story.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:38.410
It details one of the SCP Foundation’s many
investigations into an anomalous object.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.210
Nothing too strange about that.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:44.530
But there’s something more to it, since
with the Foundation there always is.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:50.210
And it has something to do with the images
at the header of each section of the entry.

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:57.230
At the top of each part of SCP-5999 is a picture
of a group of candles, seven to be exact.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:02.620
But the further down you read, one by one
the candles start to go out, until you reach

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:05.669
the end of SCP-5999.

00:05:05.669 --> 00:05:11.590
Delving into the first of these sections,
the SCP-5999 entry describes a corpse that

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:15.390
seems to be cursed with multiple anomalous
properties.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:20.380
After the assault and murder of one Ms Jacqueline
Holcroft, her remains were scattered.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:25.050
According to the entry, any person coming
into contact with a part of Ms Holcroft’s

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:30.580
deceased body, or anyone who learns about
what caused her death, will experience anomalous

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:31.740
effects.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:36.380
These manifest in various ways, for example,
subjects may hallucinate that they see a disheveled

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:40.680
woman with wounds similar to Ms Holcroft’s
before her dismemberment.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:45.280
This sight is sometimes accompanied by sounds
of whispering and even begging that calls

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.810
the subject seeing and hearing things by their
name.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:53.539
Others have reported hearing an unknown song
set to the tune of ‘Twinkle, Twinkle Little

00:05:53.539 --> 00:05:54.539
Star’.

00:05:54.539 --> 00:05:58.590
The anomalous influence of Ms Holcroft’s
dismembered remains is known to continue until

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:03.280
a subject’s death, with many reporting seeing
the woman’s deceased body lurking in their

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.490
old photos or suffering sleep paralysis as
they feel something being forcibly removed

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:09.919
from their guts.

00:06:09.919 --> 00:06:14.699
Some subjects even report discovering body
parts and organs, anything from fingers to

00:06:14.699 --> 00:06:20.460
eyes, to teeth and hair, and finding it at
random places such as when opening a drawer

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:21.479
or in their food.

00:06:21.479 --> 00:06:25.830
Finally, a number of subjects affected by
the remains of Ms Holcroft have reported a

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:31.539
specific irrational fear, the fear that the
chains are weakening.

00:06:31.539 --> 00:06:35.729
Even after the Foundation recovered Jacqueline
Holcroft’s bones and her remains were buried

00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:40.509
in a proper funeral, the effects that her
dead body parts had over living subjects did

00:06:40.509 --> 00:06:42.139
not stop.

00:06:42.139 --> 00:06:46.440
Subjects reported their children went missing,
and the attendees at Ms Holcroft’s funeral

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:50.530
were somehow spontaneously disemboweled after
the ceremony.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:55.169
To keep these effects to a minimum, the Foundation
apparently has a containment procedure in

00:06:55.169 --> 00:06:56.169
place.

00:06:56.169 --> 00:07:02.629
The SCP-5999 entry details something called
‘Procedure Sevenfold’, wherein the SCP

00:07:02.629 --> 00:07:08.139
Foundation gathers seven civilians and brings
them to a location called Albright Manor.

00:07:08.139 --> 00:07:14.360
On October 30th, these seven people are sedated
and awake on the night of October 31st.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:19.039
All entrances to Albright Manor are sealed,
trapping the civilians inside.

00:07:19.039 --> 00:07:23.830
Observed via a network of surveillance devices
throughout the Manor, Procedure Sevenfold

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:28.530
always results in the deaths of the seven
civilian witnesses brought in by the Foundation.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:33.819
Whether they are told to perform a ritual,
or are offered as a sacrifice, is unclear.

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:38.370
The following morning, Foundation clean-up
crews will remove the remains of these people,

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:40.650
disposing of their bodies with an incinerator.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:45.949
For the rest of the year, until Procedure
Sevenfold needs to be conducted again, Foundation

00:07:45.949 --> 00:07:51.530
personnel on site at Albright Manor are instructed
to be careful around any surfaces that contain

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:55.099
the phrase “This is where I died.”

00:07:55.099 --> 00:07:59.960
By now, you are most likely wondering what
the remains of Ms Holcroft and Procedure Sevenfold

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:03.169
have to do with anything we’ve talked about
so far.

00:08:03.169 --> 00:08:06.979
What is the connection to SCP-001, The Database?

00:08:06.979 --> 00:08:11.240
Is there something linking an anomalous corpse
with the Foundation’s knowledge of its own

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.750
fictional existence?

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:15.860
What does “a fear of the chains weakening”
mean?

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:20.470
And why do none of these questions seem to
acknowledge what those seven candles represent,

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:23.270
or why they’re still gradually going out?

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:28.180
Scrolling further through SCP-5999 doesn’t
seem to yield many more answers though.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:33.560
In fact, the more of the sections you look
into, the less it seems to be about Ms Holcroft,

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:35.930
or even make any link to The Database.

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:39.880
And the deeper you go, the fewer candles remain
lit.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:45.480
The next few portions of the SCP-5999 entry
are dedicated to completely different investigations

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:48.850
that have little to nothing to do with Procedure
Sevenfold.

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:53.770
Ms Holcroft’s corpse and the anomalous effects
it creates are also absent in the later segments

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:55.930
of this entry in the SCP Archive.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:09:03.270
So, if the cursed body parts of Jacqueline
Holcroft are not SCP-5999, then what is?

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:07.910
One report details the fates of a Mobile Task
Force, trapped in a fog shrouded town.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:13.670
Here, they encounter a lamb that appears to
be undead, and devolves into an ungodly winged

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:17.050
beast before the MTF team’s very eyes.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:19.990
Another that follows, is a transcript of an
exorcism.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:24.890
During a classified Foundation operation,
one Agent Grace was possessed by a demonic

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:28.320
entity, and sent to the Department of Demonology.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:33.950
Specialist in Demonic Psychology Doctor Peter
MacNeill attempted to remove the demon inhabiting

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:34.950
Agent Grace.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:39.610
However, after trying to intimidate the demonic
entity with various passages from biblical

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:44.880
texts, it appears as though maybe the demon
was able to spread its influence to both Agent

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:47.220
Grace and Doctor MacNeill.

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:51.950
Of course, neither of these reports seem to
answer any of the pressing questions, or explain

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:55.920
the exact nature of SCP-5999.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.740
As you go further into the entry, you can’t
help but notice how often chains are referenced.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:06.980
In fact, that seemed to be the one thing constant
in all these disjointed segments.

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:11.360
Mentions of a “failure of the chains to
hold what lies beneath”, and chains that

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:16.380
have become “too few in number to hold it”
all create the sense that something once was

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:21.500
locked up, sealed securely away, is managing
to break free.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:27.220
Then, finally, as the last candle goes out,
you are literally brought face-to-face with

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:33.230
the horror of SCP-5999, and its true nature
is revealed to you.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:37.410
A decaying, desiccated corpse stares out of
the screen at you.

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:42.889
Its eyes are sunken deep into its skull, lips
shriveled almost completely away, exposing

00:10:42.889 --> 00:10:45.139
rows of rotten teeth.

00:10:45.139 --> 00:10:46.750
Could it be Ms Holcroft’s body?

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.300
You aren’t sure.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:53.770
What you are sure of, is the corpse’s face
is getting closer to the screen, and now…

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.820
it’s smiling at you.

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:59.470
You can feel your heart pounding, beating
against your ribcage.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:05.180
As the world around you begins to fade, and
your life slips away from you, the last thing

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:11.330
you see is the grim face of the corpse staring
out at you with it’s dead, sunken eyes.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:17.010
The truth of SCP-5999 is that it has been
specifically designed to kill whoever reads

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:18.010
it.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:19.339
By whom, you may be asking?

00:11:19.339 --> 00:11:22.070
By the SCP Foundation themselves.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:26.730
Cast your mind back to The Database and remember
that the Overseer Council are aware of their

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:28.380
own fictional existence.

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:33.270
They know that they aren’t real, and plan
to use a memetic kill agent to take out the

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:36.970
SCP Wiki authors that created them.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:44.920
SCP-5999 is that kill agent, an entity created
by fiction to kill those living in reality.

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:51.350
SCP-5999 works by drawing a person in, offering
disjointed and disconnected horror stories

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:54.340
as a means of grabbing a reader’s attention.

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:59.600
Further and further down through the entry
that person will go, searching for the meaning

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:01.860
behind these chilling tales.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:04.050
And therein lies the trap.

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:11.610
Each layer, each section of SCP-5999 that
you read is another candle extinguished.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:18.269
And with every flame that goes out, a seal
broken, a chain becomes unbound, allowing

00:12:18.269 --> 00:12:22.810
the entity contained within the archive entry
itself to get closer.

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:28.830
Its sole purpose is to fulfil the proposal
laid out by the O5 Council after they learned

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:33.709
that they were fictional, along with the entire
SCP universe.

00:12:33.709 --> 00:12:41.209
By pulling you in with the mystery and intrigue
of the confusing, convoluted stories, SCP-5999

00:12:41.209 --> 00:12:46.310
is able to deploy, jumping out of the screen
towards you, condemning you to a dark and

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:47.839
grisly fate.

00:12:47.839 --> 00:12:52.950
Or maybe that’s just what the O5 Council
and the SCP Foundation wants us to think.

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:59.290
Either way, it might just be safer to get
your SCP knowledge here at SCP Explained.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:00.730
And speaking of…

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:04.440
Go check out “SCP-1730 - What Happened to
Site-13?

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:11.519
The Full Story Compilation” and “SCP-5545
- Mysterious Tunnels in Antarctica - ABNORMALITY”

00:13:11.519 --> 00:13:13.620
for more terrifying tales.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.930
But at least these ones won’t kill you.

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:16.430
Probably...

